===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|philosophy}} Of or pertaining to the philosophical system of {{w|Georg Wilhelm Friedrich Hegel}} (1770–1831).
#* {{RQ:Conrad Notes on Life and Letters|chapter=The Crime of Partition|pages=165–166|pageref=166|passage=The Germanic Tribes had told the whole world in all possible tones carrying conviction, the gently persuasive, the coldly logical; in tones '''Hegelian''', Nietzschean, warlike, pious, cynical, inspired, what they were going to do to the inferior races of the earth, so full of sin and all unworthiness.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-GB|author=Andrew Anthony|title=Liberalism and Its Discontents by Francis Fukuyama review – a defence of liberalism… from a former neocon|work=The Guardian|date=2022-03-08|url=https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/mar/08/liberalism-and-its-discontents-by-francis-fukuyama-review-a-defence-of-liberalism-from-a-former-neocon|issn=0261-3077|passage=As events such as 9/11, the Afghan and Iraq wars and the 2008 financial crisis took their toll on liberalism’s self-confidence, Fukuyama’s work was denounced as the height of '''Hegelian''' hubris.}}

